<section image-layout="blank" id="lE9aTa1jBn"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="sVdfkAxAyq" padding="0" colspan="21"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/tgrawnBvaSO68WfZUhbuN.png" saved-media-id="5gl5p6w35c9gsuw" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="dialectical-paper-assemblage" alt="Editorial cut-paper assemblage photographed on warm ivory paper (#FAF4E8), with crisp folded planes, subtle paper fiber and long soft daylight shadows, using vermilion #A13D32, blue slate #345F67 and ochre #B3822D with carbon-black details, no text or lettering. Three connected conceptual objects—a folded category grid, a mirrored human profile, and a small civic table—belong to one branching paper structure." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="36FDp275OX" vertical-align="start" colspan="39"><p role="eyebrow">A focused route through a larger system</p><h2>From a pressured idea to social freedom</h2><p font-size="18pt">Hegel (1770–1831) writes on logic, nature, art, religion, and history. Here we follow one path through that larger system:</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 28pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="fKWtvbY3hZ" padding="5pt 0"><h4>Dialectic</h4><p font-size="16pt">Test a determinate position through its own consequences.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hlcx5g3krF" padding="5pt 0"><h4>Aufhebung</h4><p font-size="16pt">Cancel a limitation while preserving what remains valid.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="kXMHNVFdUf" padding="5pt 0"><h4>Recognition</h4><p font-size="16pt">Understand freedom as requiring another independent self.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Qo1UdKMp5A" padding="5pt 0"><h4>Social freedom</h4><p font-size="16pt">Ask how practices and institutions can enable agency.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="11pt"><span text-color="muted">Source:</span> <a href="https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/hegel/">Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “Hegel”</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>